//RS     // ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//RS     // D-DYNARRAY1 (ratified 2026-07-01): `View<T>` zero-copy windows
//RS     // (`list.view(a..b)`).
//RS     //
//RS     // A view's Rust value is a genuine borrowed slice (`&[T]`, elided
//RS     // lifetime — see `Context::rust_type`'s `View` arm) so it is exactly as
//RS     // sound as an arena view. List, arena, string, buffer, and matrix windows
//RS     // share one provenance graph; only product diagnostics and lowering flags
//RS     // differ.
//RS     //
//RS     // E2305 fires when a declared view reaches another view boundary:
//RS     // returned, rebound to another declared view, or stored in a declared view
//RS     // field. A read-only view entering an owning destination materializes by
//RS     // default; `copies: .Explicit` restores the explicit-copy diagnostic.
//RS     // Crossing a task/channel boundary is instead caught by the general
//RS     // sendability check (`SendProblemKind::ViewBorrow` on `Type::Apply {
//RS     // name: "View", .. }`, reported as E1102) — no tracking is needed there,
//RS     // the value's TYPE alone is enough.
//RS     // ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
