//RS 
//RS     /// Every path inside `ty` that ends at a view window, with its access.
//RS     ///
//RS     /// Paths depend on the route taken, so the walk backtracks over its
//RS     /// active nominals. A nominal that cannot reach any window contributes
//RS     /// no path, so it is skipped without descending: that answer is a plain
//RS     /// reachability fact, computed once per nominal. Without the skip, a
//RS     /// large mutually recursive graph with no windows (a compiler's AST) is
//RS     /// walked once per path, which is exponential.
